{
  "dn16:0.1": "Long Discourses 16 ",
  "dn16:0.2": "The Great Discourse on the Buddha’s Extinguishment ",
  "dn16:1.1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "dn16:1.1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha, on the Vulture’s Peak Mountain. ",
  "dn16:1.1.3": "Now at that time King Ajātasattu of Magadha, son of the princess of Videha, wanted to invade the Vajjis. ",
  "dn16:1.1.4": "He said: ",
  "dn16:1.1.5": "“I shall wipe out these Vajjis, so mighty and powerful! I shall destroy them, and lay ruin and devastation upon them!” ",
  "dn16:1.2.1": "And then King Ajātasattu addressed Vassakāra the brahmin, a chief minister of Magadha, ",
  "dn16:1.2.2": "“Please, brahmin, go to the Buddha, and in my name bow with your head to his feet. Ask him if he is healthy and well, nimble, strong, and living comfortably. ",
  "dn16:1.2.3": "",
  "dn16:1.2.4": "And then say: ",
  "dn16:1.2.5": "‘Sir, King Ajātasattu of Magadha, son of the princess of Videha, wants to invade the Vajjis. ",
  "dn16:1.2.6": "He says, ",
  "dn16:1.2.7": "“I shall wipe out these Vajjis, so mighty and powerful! I shall destroy them, and lay ruin and devastation upon them!”’ ",
  "dn16:1.2.8": "Remember well how the Buddha answers and tell it to me. ",
  "dn16:1.2.9": "For Realized Ones say nothing that is not so.” ",
  "dn16:1.3.0": "1. The Brahmin Vassakāra ",
  "dn16:1.3.1": "“Yes, worthy sir,” Vassakāra replied. He had the finest carriages harnessed. Then he mounted a fine carriage and, along with other fine car